{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a630e20d55bf3105", "type": "tool_result", "content": "=== arxiv (5 results) ===\n  1. Controlling Contrastive Self-Supervised Learning with Knowledge-Driven Multiple Hypothesis: Application to Beat Tracking\n     https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.25560\n     [authors=Antonin Gagnere, Slim Essid, Geoffroy Peeters | published=2025-10-29 | primary_category=cs.SD | id=2510.25560]\n  2. A Contrastive Self-Supervised Learning scheme for beat tracking amenable to few-shot learning\n     https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.04152\n     [authors=Antonin Gagnere, Geoffroy Peeters, Slim Essid | published=2024-11-06 | primary_category=eess.AS | id=2411.04152]\n  3. The SMC Blind Spot: A Failure Mode Analysis of State-of-the-Art Beat Tracking\n     https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.12287\n     [authors=Jaehoon Ahn, Tae Gum Hwang, Moon-Ryul Jung | published=2026-05-12 | primary_category=eess.AS | id=2605.12287]\n  4. SelfMatch: Combining Contrastive Self-Supervision and Consistency for Semi-Supervised Learning\n     https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.06480\n     [authors=Byoungjip Kim, Jinho Choo, Yeong-Dae Kwon, Seongho Joe, Seungjai Min, Youngjune Gwon | published=2021-01-16 | primary_category=cs.LG | id=2101.06480]\n  5. Self-Supervised Beat Tracking in Musical Signals with Polyphonic Contrastive Learning\n     https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.01771\n     [authors=Dorian Desblancs | published=2022-01-05 | primary_category=cs.SD | id=2201.01771]\n\n=== dblp (1 results) ===\n  1. Controlling Contrastive Self-Supervised Learning with Knowledge-Driven Multiple Hypothesis: Application to Beat Tracking\n     https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.25560\n     [authors=Antonin Gagneré, Slim Essid, Geoffroy Peeters | rank=1]\n\n=== openreview (5 results) ===\n  1. A Contrastive Self-Supervised Learning Scheme for Beat Tracking Amenable to Few-Shot Learning\n     https://openreview.net/forum?id=sZZywV3WWg\n     [authors=Antonin Gagneré, Sli